{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Silo\/tutorials\/Silo\/ReactiveDependencies"},"hierarchy":{"reference":"doc:\/\/Silo\/tutorials\/Silo","paths":[["doc:\/\/Silo\/tutorials\/Silo","doc:\/\/Silo\/tutorials\/Silo\/$volume","doc:\/\/Silo\/tutorials\/Silo\/Reactive-Dependencies"],["doc:\/\/Silo\/documentation\/Silo"]],"modules":[{"reference":"doc:\/\/Silo\/tutorials\/Silo\/Your-First-Data-Source","projects":[{"sections":[{"reference":"doc:\/\/Silo\/tutorials\/Silo\/BuildingAD6DiceRoller#Creating-the-Data-Source","kind":"task"},{"reference":"doc:\/\/Silo\/tutorials\/Silo\/BuildingAD6DiceRoller#Building-the-Dice-View","kind":"task"},{"kind":"task","reference":"doc:\/\/Silo\/tutorials\/Silo\/BuildingAD6DiceRoller#Rolling-Automatically"},{"kind":"assessment","reference":"doc:\/\/Silo\/tutorials\/Silo\/BuildingAD6DiceRoller#Check-Your-Understanding"}],"reference":"doc:\/\/Silo\/tutorials\/Silo\/BuildingAD6DiceRoller"}]},{"reference":"doc:\/\/Silo\/tutorials\/Silo\/Reactive-Dependencies","projects":[{"sections":[{"reference":"doc:\/\/Silo\/tutorials\/Silo\/ReactiveDependencies#Setting-Up-the-Dice-Service","kind":"task"},{"reference":"doc:\/\/Silo\/tutorials\/Silo\/ReactiveDependencies#Choosing-the-Right-Refresh-Policy","kind":"task"},{"kind":"task","reference":"doc:\/\/Silo\/tutorials\/Silo\/ReactiveDependencies#Adding-a-Second-Dependency"},{"kind":"task","reference":"doc:\/\/Silo\/tutorials\/Silo\/ReactiveDependencies#Bridging-Streams-to-SwiftUI"},{"kind":"task","reference":"doc:\/\/Silo\/tutorials\/Silo\/ReactiveDependencies#Building-the-Roll-View"},{"kind":"assessment","reference":"doc:\/\/Silo\/tutorials\/Silo\/ReactiveDependencies#Check-Your-Understanding"}],"reference":"doc:\/\/Silo\/tutorials\/Silo\/ReactiveDependencies"}]}]},"sections":[{"estimatedTimeInMinutes":30,"kind":"hero","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Build a configurable dice roller that automatically re-rolls whenever the player changes the dice type or count. You will learn how to declare dependencies, choose the right refresh policy, and wire SwiftUI pickers to reactive streams — resulting in a fully functional application."}]}],"title":"Reacting to Dice Configuration","chapter":"Reactive Dependencies"},{"kind":"tasks","tasks":[{"contentSection":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Begin from the same pattern as Tutorial 1 — a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DiceService"},{"text":" that rolls a single D6. The fetch is identical; what changes is where the range comes from.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Currently, the range ","type":"text"},{"code":"1...6","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is hardcoded. The objective is to replace it with a value that arrives from an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AsyncStream<Int>"},{"type":"text","text":". When that stream emits a new number of sides, the data source re-rolls automatically. Silo calls this upstream stream a "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"dependency"}]},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"contentAndMedia","mediaPosition":"trailing"}],"stepsSection":[{"caption":[],"media":null,"runtimePreview":null,"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Create "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DiceService.swift"},{"type":"text","text":". The structure mirrors "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DiceRoller"},{"type":"text","text":" from Tutorial 1 — a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DataSource<[Int]>"},{"type":"text","text":" whose fetch returns a single random roll. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[Int]"},{"text":" is an ","type":"text"},{"code":"Array","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so no ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"emptyValue"},{"text":" is needed.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"code":"DiceService-01.swift","type":"step"},{"caption":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"With "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".eager"},{"type":"text","text":", Silo re-rolls immediately whenever "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sides"},{"type":"text","text":" emits, even before any subscriber has appeared on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"rolls.values"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"code":"DiceService-02.swift","runtimePreview":null,"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Accept a "},{"code":"sides: AsyncStream<Int>","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" in the initialiser. Wrap it with "},{"code":".dependency(.eager)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and pass it to "},{"code":"dataSource()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". The fetch closure now receives the current sides value as a parameter — replace the hardcoded "},{"code":"6","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with the stream’s current value.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"step","media":null}],"anchor":"Setting-Up-the-Dice-Service","title":"Setting Up the Dice Service"},{"stepsSection":[{"type":"step","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Change "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".dependency(.eager)"},{"type":"text","text":" to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".dependency(.lazy)"},{"type":"text","text":". This single word controls when Silo re-rolls relative to subscriber presence."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"caption":[],"media":null,"runtimePreview":null,"code":"DiceService-03.swift"},{"type":"step","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"clear: true"},{"type":"text","text":" to the dependency. When the dice type changes, Silo immediately emits an empty array before the new roll arrives — so the view never shows D6 results while a D20 roll is in flight."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"caption":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Without ","type":"text"},{"code":"clear: true","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the previous results remain visible until replaced by the new ones. For a dice type change, this is confusing; for other dependencies, retaining the previous value during the transition may be preferable. This distinction is explored in the next section.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"media":null,"runtimePreview":null,"code":"DiceService-04.swift"}],"title":"Choosing the Right Refresh Policy","contentSection":[{"mediaPosition":"trailing","kind":"contentAndMedia","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"code":".eager","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" policy re-rolls even when no view is watching, resulting in unnecessary computation. Switch to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".lazy"},{"type":"text","text":" so re-rolls only happen while an active subscriber is present."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":".lazy","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" defers the re-roll rather than dropping it. If "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sides"},{"type":"text","text":" emits while no subscriber is present, Silo remembers the pending change and fires the re-roll the moment the first subscriber arrives — results are always current when the view appears."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"anchor":"Choosing-the-Right-Refresh-Policy"},{"stepsSection":[{"caption":[],"media":null,"runtimePreview":null,"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Add ","type":"text"},{"code":"count: AsyncStream<Int>","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" alongside "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sides"},{"type":"text","text":". Pass both to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dataSource()"},{"type":"text","text":" as separate dependency arguments. The fetch closure now receives both "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sides"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"count"},{"type":"text","text":"; use them to produce the full set of rolls."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"code":"DiceService-05.swift","type":"step"}],"title":"Adding a Second Dependency","contentSection":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"count"},{"type":"text","text":" stream so the player can roll multiple dice at once. When either "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sides"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"count"},{"type":"text","text":" changes, the service re-rolls. Both values are delivered to the fetch closure simultaneously."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Silo holds the first re-roll until ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"all","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" dependencies have emitted at least once. The fetch closure is always called with a complete, valid set of inputs.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Note that "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"count"},{"type":"text","text":" omits "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"clear: true"},{"type":"text","text":". Changing from 2d20 to 3d20 keeps the previous two rolls visible while the new set loads — a less disruptive transition. Changing the dice type ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sides"},{"type":"text","text":") still clears immediately because previous results are irrelevant for a different die."}]}],"mediaPosition":"trailing","kind":"contentAndMedia"}],"anchor":"Adding-a-Second-Dependency"},{"contentSection":[{"kind":"contentAndMedia","mediaPosition":"trailing","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DiceService"},{"type":"text","text":" is driven by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AsyncStream"},{"type":"text","text":" values, not SwiftUI state. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RollViewModel"},{"text":" owns the streams and acts as the bridge: it creates stream\/continuation pairs, initialises ","type":"text"},{"code":"DiceService","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with them, and exposes simple methods for the view to call.","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AsyncStream.makeStream(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":" returns both the stream (the read-end, passed to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DiceService"},{"type":"text","text":") and the continuation (the write-end, kept by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RollViewModel"},{"type":"text","text":"). Calling "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".yield()"},{"type":"text","text":" on a continuation pushes a new value into the stream, triggering a re-roll."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Seeding initial values in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"init"},{"type":"text","text":" is important: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DiceService"},{"type":"text","text":" will not make its first roll until both dependencies have emitted at least once. Yielding "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"6"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"1"},{"type":"text","text":" immediately ensures the first roll happens as soon as the view subscribes."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"stepsSection":[{"code":"RollViewModel-01.swift","runtimePreview":null,"type":"step","media":null,"caption":[],"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Create "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RollViewModel.swift"},{"type":"text","text":". Use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AsyncStream.makeStream(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":" to create stream\/continuation pairs for "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sides"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"count"},{"type":"text","text":". Initialise "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DiceService"},{"type":"text","text":" with the streams, then immediately yield the starting values so both dependencies emit before the view appears."}]}]},{"code":"RollViewModel-02.swift","runtimePreview":null,"type":"step","media":null,"caption":[],"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"selectSides(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"selectCount(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" methods that call "},{"code":".yield()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" on the appropriate continuation. Also make "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"service"},{"text":" private and expose ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"rolls"},{"text":" as a computed property and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reroll()"},{"text":" as a convenience method — the view has no need to access the service directly.","type":"text"}]}]}],"anchor":"Bridging-Streams-to-SwiftUI","title":"Bridging Streams to SwiftUI"},{"title":"Building the Roll View","contentSection":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Build the SwiftUI view around "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RollViewModel"},{"text":". Because ","type":"text"},{"code":"RollViewModel","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" owns both the streams and the ","type":"text"},{"code":"DiceService","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"RollView","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" needs no parameters — "},{"code":"@State private var viewModel = RollViewModel()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is the only initialisation required and the view compiles standalone at every step."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The Re-roll button calls "},{"code":"viewModel.reroll()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which in turn calls ","type":"text"},{"code":"refresh(clear: true)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on the data source. This is the same pattern from Tutorial 1, now applied alongside automatic dependency-driven re-rolls.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"contentAndMedia","mediaPosition":"trailing"}],"stepsSection":[{"media":null,"caption":[],"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Create "},{"code":"RollView.swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" with a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RollViewModel"},{"type":"text","text":" stored in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":". The view is already fully self-contained and can be previewed."}]}],"runtimePreview":"RollView-01.png","code":"RollView-01.swift","type":"step"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Add ","type":"text"},{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" properties for ","type":"text"},{"code":"rolls","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"isRolling","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Subscribe to ","type":"text"},{"code":"viewModel.rolls.valueWithState","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in ","type":"text"},{"code":".task","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Display each die result in a ","type":"text"},{"code":"List","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with a running total, a ","type":"text"},{"code":"ProgressView","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" overlay for the initial load, and a Re-roll button pinned to the bottom that calls ","type":"text"},{"code":"viewModel.reroll()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"step","code":"RollView-02.swift","caption":[],"media":null,"runtimePreview":"RollView-02.png"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Add ","type":"text"},{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" properties for ","type":"text"},{"code":"selectedSides","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"selectedCount","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Move the rolls into their own ","type":"text"},{"code":"Section","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and add a "},{"code":"\"Configuration\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" section above it containing two "},{"code":"Picker","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" rows. Inside a "},{"code":"List","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Picker","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" renders as a tappable row that shows the current value inline — no toolbar is needed. The pickers update SwiftUI state, but do not yet feed into ","type":"text"},{"code":"RollViewModel","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — the dice configuration does not change until the final step.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"step","code":"RollView-03.swift","caption":[],"media":null,"runtimePreview":"RollView-03.png"},{"code":"RollView-04.swift","runtimePreview":"RollView-04.png","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Add ","type":"text"},{"code":".onChange","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" modifiers for ","type":"text"},{"code":"selectedSides","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"selectedCount","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" that call ","type":"text"},{"code":"viewModel.selectSides","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"viewModel.selectCount","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Each call yields a new value into the stream, which triggers an automatic re-roll — completing the SwiftUI picker → continuation → dependency → re-roll loop.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"step","caption":[],"media":null}],"anchor":"Building-the-Roll-View"}]},{"anchor":"Check-Your-Understanding","kind":"assessments","assessments":[{"choices":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Immediately when the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DataSource"},{"type":"text","text":" is created by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".build()"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}],"justification":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".eager"},{"text":" policy re-rolls as soon as the dependency emits, regardless of subscribers. With ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".lazy"},{"text":", no roll happens until a subscriber arrives.","type":"text"}]}],"isCorrect":false},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The first time ","type":"text"},{"code":"refresh()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is called manually.","type":"text"}]}],"isCorrect":false,"justification":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"With "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".lazy"},{"type":"text","text":", the first roll is triggered automatically when the first subscriber appears — calling "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"refresh()"},{"type":"text","text":" manually is not required."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"When the first subscriber appears on ","type":"text"},{"code":"values","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"valueWithState","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}],"isCorrect":true,"justification":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":".lazy"},{"type":"text","text":" defers the roll until a subscriber is present. If the dependency already emitted before the subscriber arrived, the pending refresh fires immediately when the first subscriber appears."}]}]}],"content":[],"title":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"With ","type":"text"},{"code":".lazy","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" policy, when does the first roll happen?","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"multiple-choice"},{"content":[],"choices":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Immediately after ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sides"},{"type":"text","text":" emits."}]}],"isCorrect":false,"justification":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The data source waits until every dependency has emitted at least once. Even though "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sides"},{"type":"text","text":" is ready, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"count"},{"type":"text","text":" must emit before the first roll can proceed."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"After ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"count"},{"text":" emits its first value, 2 seconds later.","type":"text"}]}],"isCorrect":true,"justification":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Silo holds the first roll until all dependencies have values. This guarantees the fetch closure always receives a complete, well-defined set of inputs.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The roll never happens — you must call ","type":"text"},{"code":"refresh()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" manually when using multiple dependencies.","type":"text"}]}],"isCorrect":false,"justification":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Multiple dependencies work just like a single dependency. Once all have emitted, the data source rolls automatically according to the configured policy.","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"multiple-choice","title":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"You have two dependencies. The ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sides"},{"text":" stream emits immediately; the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"count"},{"text":" stream takes 2 seconds to emit its first value. When does the first roll happen?","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[],"choices":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Changing dice type shows a loading indicator while new results load; changing dice count keeps the previous rolls visible until new ones arrive.","type":"text"}]}],"justification":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"clear: true"},{"type":"text","text":" on the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sides"},{"type":"text","text":" dependency immediately empties the cached results, so the view transitions to its “empty + refreshing” state and shows a loading indicator. Without "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"clear: true"},{"type":"text","text":", the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"count"},{"type":"text","text":" change leaves the previous rolls in place — a less disruptive transition when only the number of dice changes."}]}],"isCorrect":true},{"justification":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The loading indicator is driven by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isRefreshing"},{"type":"text","text":", not by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"clear: true"},{"type":"text","text":". "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"clear: true"},{"type":"text","text":" controls whether the previous "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"value"}]},{"type":"text","text":" is cleared; the source is marked as refreshing for any in-flight fetch regardless."}]}],"isCorrect":false,"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Both changes show a loading indicator — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"clear: true"},{"type":"text","text":" is required for the loading indicator to work at all."}]}]},{"justification":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"isRefreshing","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is part of ","type":"text"},{"code":"DataSourceState","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and is delivered by the ","type":"text"},{"code":"valueWithState","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" stream for every in-flight fetch. The ","type":"text"},{"code":"isRolling","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" state property in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RollView"},{"type":"text","text":" is driven directly by it."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"isCorrect":false,"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Neither change shows a loading indicator — a separate state variable would be required to track that."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"title":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sides"},{"type":"text","text":" uses "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".dependency(.lazy, clear: true)"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"count"},{"type":"text","text":" uses "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".dependency(.lazy)"},{"type":"text","text":". What is the visible difference in the UI when the player changes dice type versus changing dice count?"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"multiple-choice"}]}],"metadata":{"title":"Reacting to Dice Configuration","category":"Silo","role":"project","categoryPathComponent":"Silo"},"kind":"project","schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/tutorials\/silo\/reactivedependencies"]}],"references":{"doc://Silo/tutorials/Silo/BuildingAD6DiceRoller#Building-the-Dice-View":{"role":"pseudoSymbol","type":"section","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"In this tutorial, you will build a D6 dice roller using Silo. The fetch is a single line — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int.random(in: 1...6)"},{"type":"text","text":" — so every concept you encounter is focused on Silo, with no boilerplate distractions."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Silo\/tutorials\/Silo\/BuildingAD6DiceRoller#Building-the-Dice-View","url":"\/tutorials\/silo\/buildingad6diceroller#Building-the-Dice-View","title":"Building the Dice View","kind":"section"},"doc://Silo/tutorials/Silo":{"role":"overview","identifier":"doc:\/\/Silo\/tutorials\/Silo","title":"Build Reactive Data Layers with Silo","abstract":[{"text":"These two hands-on tutorials take you from a basic data source to a fully reactive, dependency-driven data layer. By the end, you will know how to handle caching, retry, auto-refresh, and upstream state changes in real SwiftUI apps.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","kind":"overview","url":"\/tutorials\/silo"},"RollView-04.png":{"variants":[{"url":"\/images\/Silo\/RollView-04.png","traits":["1x","light"]}],"identifier":"RollView-04.png","type":"image","alt":"Roll view showing four D12 results with a total, and the Configuration section showing D12 and 4 selected"},"doc://Silo/tutorials/Silo/ReactiveDependencies#Adding-a-Second-Dependency":{"title":"Adding a Second Dependency","kind":"section","abstract":[{"text":"Build a configurable dice roller that automatically re-rolls whenever the player changes the dice type or count. You will learn how to declare dependencies, choose the right refresh policy, and wire SwiftUI pickers to reactive streams — resulting in a fully functional application.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/tutorials\/silo\/reactivedependencies#Adding-a-Second-Dependency","type":"section","identifier":"doc:\/\/Silo\/tutorials\/Silo\/ReactiveDependencies#Adding-a-Second-Dependency","role":"pseudoSymbol"},"RollViewModel-02.swift":{"fileName":"RollViewModel.swift","fileType":"swift","syntax":"swift","content":["import Silo","","@MainActor","final class RollViewModel {","    var rolls: DataSource<[Int]> { service.rolls }","","    private let service: DiceService","    private let sidesContinuation: AsyncStream<Int>.Continuation","    private let countContinuation: AsyncStream<Int>.Continuation","","    init() {","        let (sidesStream, sidesCont) = AsyncStream.makeStream(of: Int.self)","        let (countStream, countCont) = AsyncStream.makeStream(of: Int.self)","        sidesContinuation = sidesCont","        countContinuation = countCont","        service = DiceService(sides: sidesStream, count: countStream)","        sidesCont.yield(6)","        countCont.yield(1)","    }","","    func selectSides(_ sides: Int) {","        sidesContinuation.yield(sides)","    }","","    func selectCount(_ count: Int) {","        countContinuation.yield(count)","    }","","    func reroll() async throws {","        try await service.rolls.refresh(clear: true)","    }","}"],"type":"file","highlights":[{"line":5},{"line":7},{"line":19},{"line":20},{"line":21},{"line":22},{"line":23},{"line":24},{"line":25},{"line":26},{"line":27},{"line":28},{"line":29},{"line":30}],"identifier":"RollViewModel-02.swift"},"RollView-04.swift":{"fileName":"RollView.swift","fileType":"swift","syntax":"swift","content":["import Silo","import SwiftUI","","struct RollView: View {","    @State private var viewModel = RollViewModel()","","    @State private var rolls: [Int] = []","    @State private var isRolling = false","    @State private var selectedSides = 6","    @State private var selectedCount = 1","","    let sideOptions = [4, 6, 8, 10, 12, 20, 100]","    let countOptions = Array(1...6)","","    var body: some View {","        List {","            Section(\"Configuration\") {","                Picker(\"Sides\", selection: $selectedSides) {","                    ForEach(sideOptions, id: \\.self) { Text(\"D\\($0)\") }","                }","                Picker(\"Count\", selection: $selectedCount) {","                    ForEach(countOptions, id: \\.self) { Text(\"\\($0)\") }","                }","            }","            Section {","                ForEach(rolls.indices, id: \\.self) { i in","                    Text(\"Die \\(i + 1): \\(rolls[i])\")","                        .font(.title2)","                }","                if rolls.count > 1 {","                    Text(\"Total: \\(rolls.reduce(0, +))\")","                        .font(.headline)","                        .foregroundStyle(.secondary)","                }","            }","        }","        .overlay {","            if isRolling && rolls.isEmpty {","                ProgressView(\"Rolling…\")","            }","        }","        .safeAreaInset(edge: .bottom) {","            Button(\"Re-roll\") {","                Task { try? await viewModel.reroll() }","            }","            .buttonStyle(.borderedProminent)","            .padding()","        }","        .onChange(of: selectedSides) { _, newValue in","            viewModel.selectSides(newValue)","        }","        .onChange(of: selectedCount) { _, newValue in","            viewModel.selectCount(newValue)","        }","        .task {","            for await snapshot in viewModel.rolls.valueWithState {","                rolls = snapshot.value","                isRolling = snapshot.state.isRefreshing","            }","        }","    }","}"],"type":"file","highlights":[{"line":49},{"line":50},{"line":51},{"line":52},{"line":53},{"line":54}],"identifier":"RollView-04.swift"},"doc://Silo/tutorials/Silo/ReactiveDependencies#Choosing-the-Right-Refresh-Policy":{"title":"Choosing the Right Refresh Policy","url":"\/tutorials\/silo\/reactivedependencies#Choosing-the-Right-Refresh-Policy","abstract":[{"text":"Build a configurable dice roller that automatically re-rolls whenever the player changes the dice type or count. You will learn how to declare dependencies, choose the right refresh policy, and wire SwiftUI pickers to reactive streams — resulting in a fully functional a